    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0197" n="1031" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1031"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112A/1855u</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Diplomatic Representatives
                        in Latin American Countries </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-05T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 5, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Inexpediency of publishing certain names eligible for enemy trading list
                    necessitates a confidential enemy trading list. In recommending additions and
                    removals confidential list confer British, French, Italian colleagues and
                    proceed as in case recommendations published enemy trading list. Specific
                    reasons within scope Trading with Enemy Act should be given in recommendations
                    for addition <pb facs="0198" n="1032" xml:id="pg1032"/> to enemy trading list or
                    confidential list. Desirable to unify Allied confidential lists far as possible.
                    Fictitious names and names of men of straw used merely to cloak enemy trade
                    should be recommended for inclusion in cloaks list and not enemy trading list,
                    indicating name of principal as well. No established firm should be listed in
                    cloaks list for cloaking enemy trade, but should be recommended for published or
                    confidential enemy trading list.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
